feature1.prompt:
Custom template tags raise TemplateSyntaxError when keyword-only arguments with defaults are provided. When creating simple tags without variable keyword args but with a keyword argument that has a default value, it is not possible to supply any other variable. For example, a simple tag defined as:

@register.simple_tag
def hello(*, greeting='hello'):
    return f'{greeting} world'

when rendered with:

{% hello greeting='hi' %}

raises the error “'hello' received unexpected keyword argument 'greeting'”. Also, supplying a keyword argument a second time, as in:

@register.simple_tag
def hi(*, greeting):
    return f'{greeting} world'

with the template usage:

{% hi greeting='hi' greeting='hello' %}

raises “'hi' received unexpected keyword argument 'greeting'” instead of the expected "'hi' received multiple values for keyword argument 'greeting'".
